claim.claim-text:
measuring a distance from a lens (24, 124) to a mark (14);
calculating a focus position for an autofocus system (132) that focuses the lens (24, 124) on the mark (14);
applying an offset to the calculated focus position to produce an offset focus position;
setting the autofocus system (132) to the offset focus position;
acquiring an image of the mark (14) with the autofocus system (132) set to the offset focus position; and
providing the image of the mark (14) to a decoder for decoding;
wherein the method further comprises determining the offset by
calculating the offset based on one or more of: a distance between dots of the mark (14), the distance from the lens (24, 124) to the mark (14), and a focus position.

a lens (24, 124);
an autofocus system (132) that manipulates the lens (24, 124) in accordance with control signals;
an image acquisition system (20, 120) that measures a distance from the lens (24, 124) to a mark (14);
a processor (100) that is programmed to:

calculate a focus position for an autofocus system (132) that focuses the lens (24, 124) on the mark;
apply an offset to the calculated focus position to produce an offset focus position;
set the autofocus system (132) to the offset focus position;
via the image acquisition system (20, 120), acquire an image of the mark (14) with the autofocus system (132) set to the offset focus position;
providing the image of the mark (14) to a decoder for decoding;
wherein the value of the offset is determined by
calculating the offset based on one or more of: a distance between dots of the mark (14), the distance from the lens (24, 124) to the mark (14), and a focus position.
